From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dj <43033058+DjDeveloperr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:32:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fprintd: bind Touch ID prints to the account they were
 enrolled for

Prints are stored under a username, and a username outlives its account:
delete an account, create another with the same name, and the new account
found the old one's prints, so the old account's finger verified as the new
one. For the Touch ID driver, each account's storage directory now keeps a
record of the account its prints belong to: its uid, an instance GUID, and
the instance each print was enrolled under. A print verifies, is listed, and
blocks a new enrolment of its finger only while the account the username
names now has the recorded uid and the print carries the recorded instance.

An enrolment for an account whose record names another uid starts a new
instance; the earlier account's print for the same finger is deleted first,
from the device and from storage, and its other prints stay unusable until
they are deleted. Deletion still reaches every stored print, so removing a
user's prints also removes those an earlier account left. Prints stored
before records existed are adopted, all together, by the account that holds
their username when a record is first needed.

Signed-off-by: Dj <43033058+DjDeveloperr@users.noreply.github.com>
